 "transcript": [
  "[action] Wang Lung looks up, surprised.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Wang Lung demands his sons account for themselves.",
  "[action] (to the second son) the second son gives account of his plans",
  "Wang Lung: \"Well, and now what am I?\"",
  "the second son (to Wang Lung): \"I have thought to have a great market in the town where the big houses are, but I have not yet a place. There are some houses which the rich can buy but not the poor like me. I have asked many times of the great merchant Liu and he says that he can get me a place if I bring him the money. He says, 'Bring me a hundred pieces of silver and I will get you a place,' and I say, 'Well, and what will I do after that?'\"",
  "the second son (to Wang Lung): \"He says, 'After that you will have to bring me a few more, so that I may keep my friend, the official, properly entertained, and the friend of my friend, the official, and the son of my friend, the official, for they must all see what a man you are and how rich you are to be able to set up a grain market in the town and in a year you will be richer than I, who have spent my life in the grain trade.'\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and and what is the eldest son?\"",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"Well, and and what is the eldest son?\"",
  "the second son (to Wang Lung): \"I do not know,\"",
  "[says] (to the eldest son) Wang Lung demands to know about his eldest son's plans.",
  "Wang Lung (to the eldest son): \"What is it that you are going to do?\"",
